$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of trans-4-tert-butoxycarbonylamino-cyclohexanecarboxylic acid
(11) (20 g, 82.2 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1.2 L) was treated with
N,O-dimethyl-hydroxylamine hydrochloride (12.83 g, 131.5 mmol, 1.6
equiv), N-methylmorpholine (10.85 mL, 98.6 mmol, 1.2 equiv) and at 0°C
with EDCI (18.91 g, 98.64 mmol, 2.2 equiv) and HOBT (12.62 g, 82.2 mmol,
1 equiv). The reaction mixture was stirred 2 h at room temperature and
extracted with aqueous 10% KHSO4 solution/Et2O (3x). The organic phases
were washed with aqueous saturated NaHCO3 solution, 10% NaCl solution and
dried over Na2SO4 to yield
trans-[4-(methoxy-methylcarbamoyl)-cyclohexyl]-carbamic acid tert-butyl
ester. Yield (24.25 g, quantitative). Mp: 130- 140°C, slowly dec. MS m/z:
287.2 (M+H+).
