$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Part A: A solution of
2-((3R,5R,6S)-1-((S)-2-(tert-butylsulfonyl)-1-cyclopropylethyl)-6-(4-chloro-3-fluorophenyl)-5-(3-chlorophenyl)-3-methy2-oxopiperidin-3-yl)acetic
acid (69)17 (22.00 g, 36.8 mmol) and glycine methyl ester hydrochloride
(11.54 g, 92 mmol) in DMF (100.0 mL) was treated with EDC (17.62 g, 92
mmol), HOAT (12.51 g, 92 mmol), and sodium hydrogencarbonate (15.44 g,
184 mmol) successively at room temperature. The reaction was stirred at
40 °C overnight. After this period, the reaction was diluted (1 N aq.
HCl), extracted (2 x EtOAc), and washed (1 x sat. aq. NaHCO3, and 2 x
brine). The combined organic layer was dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The product of this step was used in the next
process without further purification.
2-(2-((3R,5R,6S)-1-((S)-2-(tert-butylsulfonyl)-1-cyclopropylethyl)-6-(4-chloro-3-fluorophenyl)-5-(3-chlorophenyl)-3-methy2-oxopiperidin-3-yl)acetamido)acetate,
yield quantitative. Mass spectrum (ESI) m/z = 669.2 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel Inhibitors of the MDM2-p53 Interaction Featuring Hydrogen Bond
Acceptors as Carboxylic Acid Isosteres
