$DATUM tert-Butyl 3-(2-methylbenzo[d]thiazol-6-ylamino)-3-oxopropylcarbamate 48
HATU (913 mg, 2.40 mmol) was added dropwise as a solution in DMF (5 mL)
to a mixture of 2-methylbenzo[d]thiazol-6-amine 37 (395 mg, 2.4 mmol),
3-(tertbutoxycarbonylamino) propanoic acid (500 mg, 2.64 mmol) and DIPEA
(0.596 mL, 3.6 mmol) in DMF (15 mL). The mixture was stirred at 22°C for
16 hours. The DMF was evaporated and the residue was diluted with EtOAc
(100 mL). The solution was washed sequentially with water (100 mL), 0.5M
ammonium chloride solution, water (100 mL), 0.5M sodium hydrogencarbonate
solution (100 mL) and saturated brine (50 mL), dried over MgSO4 and
evaporated. tert-butyl
3-(2-methylbenzo[d]thiazol-6-ylamino)-3-oxopropylcarbamate (801 mg, 99 %)
as a light brown foam. 1H NMR (400 MHz, d6-DMSO, 30°C) δ 1.39 (9H, s),
2.49-2.55 (2H, m), 2.76 (3H, s), 3.25 (2H, dt), 6.84 (1H, br.s), 7.51
(1H, dd), 7.82 (1H, d), 8.40 (1H, d), 10.11 (1H, s). m/z (ES+), (M+H)+ =
336.2; 5 minute acidic method, HPLC tR = 1.82 min.
