$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N,4-Dimethoxy-N-cis/trans-methylcyclohexanecarboxamide (6).
1,1'-Carbonylbis-1H-imidazole (6.8 g, 74 mmol) was added portion-wise to
a mixture of 4-methoxycyclohexanecarboxylic acid (10 g, 63 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (200 mL). The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 1 h.
N,O-dimethylhydroxylaminehydrochloride (6.8 g, 74 mmol) was added. The
mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight, poured into H2O and
extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was separated, washed three
times with H2O, dried, filtered and concentrated.
N,4-Dimethoxy-N-cis/trans-methylcyclohexanecarboxamide, as colorless oil
(4:1 cis/trans mixture), yield 12.6 g, 99%. 1H NMR: δ 1.10-1.60 (m, 4H),
1.80-2.20 (m, 4H), 2.6-2.8 (m, 1H,), 3.18 (s, 3H) 3.18-3.37 (m, 1H), 3.31
(s, 3H), 3.75 (s, 3H).
