$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-(4-[N-(2-Phenoxy-2-oxoethylcarbamoyl]aminomethyl]-3-methylbenzoyl)-2,3,4,5-tetrahydro-1H-1-benzazepine
(19f). To a solution of 19a (0.134 g, 0.33 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (25 mL) were
added phenol (0.155 g, 1.6 mmol), 4-(dimethylamino)pyridine (0.04 g, 0.33
mmol), and WSCDI (0.135 mg, 0.66 mmol). The mixture was stirred at reflux
for 48 h and cooled. The mixture was washed with 1 M KHSO4, saturated
NaHCO3 solution and brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo.
The crude material was purified by chromatography (eluant EtOAc:pet.
ether 80:20) to give a white solid; yield 0.038 g (33%).
1-(4-[N-(2-Benzylamino-2-oxoethylcarbamoyl]aminomethyl]-3-methylbenzoyl)-2,3,4,5-tetrahydro-1H-1-benzazepine
(19i). Using the same procedure as 19f, 19a was reacted with benzylamine
to give a white solid; yield 0.12 g (99%). 1H NMR δ 1.40-1.60 (1H, m),
1.86-2.20 (3H, m), 2.12 (3H, s), 2.70-3.10 (3H, m), 3.76 (2H, s), 4.17
(2H, s), 4.35 (2H, s), 4.94 (1H, d, J=13.9 Hz), 5.82 (1H, br s), 5.89
(1H, br s), 6.61 (1H, d, J=7.6 Hz), 6.78-6.96 (4H, m), 6.98-7.10 (2H, m),
7.14-7.36 (5H, m), 7.46 (1H, br s). HRMS: 485.2549 (calculated) and
485.2380 (observed).
