$DATUM (3bS,4aR)-N-(2-Methoxybenzyl)-3,4,4-trimethyl-3b,4,4a,5-tetrahydrocyclopropa
[3,4]cyclopenta[1, 2-c]thiophene-1-carboxamide (9). A solution of
(3bS,4aR)-3,4,4-trimethyl-3b,4,4a,5-tetrahydrocyclo-propa
[3,4]cyclopenta[1,2-c]thiophene-1-carboxylic acid 20 (30.0 mg, 135 μmol),
TBTU (47.7 mg, 148 μmol), and Hunig s base (57.6 mg, 445 μmol) in DMF
(1.2 mL) was stirred at rt for 30 min before a solution of
2-methoxy-benzylamine (3.3 mg, 0.022 mmol) in DMF (0.2 mL) was added. The
mixture was allowed to stand at rt for 1 h before it was subjected to
purification by preparative HPLC (Grom-Sil 120 ODS-4-HE, 30 mm × 75 mm,
10 μm particle size, gradient of 20-95% acetonitrile in water containing
0.5% formic acid). 9 (45 mg, 98%) as a colorless lyophilizate. LC-MS: tR
= 1.08 min, [M + 1]+ = 342.18 (calcd 342.15). 1H NMR (H6-DMSO, solvent
suppression): δ 7.64 (t br, J = 4.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.17 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 1 H),
7.06 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1 H), 6.83 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.32 (d, J = 5.2
Hz, 2 H), 3.79 (s, 3 H), 2.93 (dd, J = 6.3, 18.3 Hz, 1 H), 2.74 (d, J =
18.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.31 (s, 3 H), 1.86-1.99 (m, 2 H), 1.08 (s, 3 H), 0.68 (s,
3 H). LC-HRMS: tR = 2.14 min, [M + H]/z = 342.1528, found 342.1530.
