$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2: Preparation of 32-2. A solution of 32-1 (1.26 g, 3.47 mmol) and
C35 (1.08 g, 3.70 mmol) in DMF (15 mL) was treated with HATU (1.45 g,
3.81 mmol) followed by Hunig's base (0.70 mL, 4.06 mmol) and allowed to
stir at ambient temperature for 13 hours. The crude reaction mixture was
diluted with water (120 mL), stirred vigorously for 45 minutes, and
filtered. The resulting precipitate was washed with water followed by
heptanes, dried under vacuum, dry loaded with celite onto an Analogix
SF40-150g silica gel column, and purified with a 40-80% EtOAc/heptanes
gradient over 8 CV to afford 32-2 as a solid. Colorless solid, yield 1.85
g, 3.37 mmol, 97%. LCMS m/z 616.4 (M+H)+.
