$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (3,4-Dinitrophenyl)morpholin-4-ylmethanone (19). A solution of
3,4-dinitrobenzoic acid 18 (10 g, 47 mmol) and DMF (0.1 mL) in THF (100
mL) was treated with thionyl chloride (4.5 mL, 62 mmol) and then heated
at reﬂux for 2.5 h. The mixture was then cooled to ~0 °C, and
triethylamine (10 mL, 71 mmol) was added over 20 min, keeping the
internal temperature at <5 °C. Morpholine (7.2 mL, 82 mmol) was added
over 15 min, keeping the internal temperature at <10 °C, and then the
mixture was allowed to warm to ambient temperature. After being stirred
overnight, the mixture was diluted with water (250 mL) and cooled in ice.
A beige solid was ﬁltered off under suction, washed with a further
portion of cold water (25 mL), and dried in vacuo to afford 19 as a
yellow solid (12.7 g, 96%) (3,4-Dinitrophenyl)morpholin-4-ylmethanone
(19), yield (12.7 g, 96%) 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6): 8.33-8.29 (m, 2H),
8.01 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 1H), 3.73-3.63 (m, 4H), 3.35-3.30 (m, 4H). LC/MS: tR
= 1.08 min, m/z = 282 [M + H]+.
