$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3 (Method B): Gemcitabine hydrochloride (100 g, 333.7 mmol
) was slurried in 300 mL of pyridine and 100 mL of acetonitrile in a 1 L
flask. The white slurry was cooled with an ice water bath to 0-10 °C.
Chlorotrimethylsilane (45.8 g, 417 mmol) was added via an addition funnel
while controlling the temperature at 0-10 °C. The resulting thin slurry
was stirred at 0-10 °C for 2.5 h to give a homogeneous solution. In a
separate flask, valproic acid (13.2 g, 91.8 mmol ) was combined with 200
mL of acetonitrile. CDI (14.8 g, 91.8 mmol) was added in portions to
control off-gassing. The resulting solution was stirred for a minimum of
30 minutes. The imidazolide solution was combined with the silylated
gemcitabine in the 1 L flask. The mixture was heated to 60 °C and stirred
for 40 hours. The reaction mixture was cooled to 40 °C and quenched with
175 mL of absolute ethanol while keeping the temperature below 50 °C.
After the mixture was stirred for 30 minutes at 40-45 °C, 50 mL of water
was added. The resulting reaction mixture was stirred at 45-50 °C for
additional 4-5 h. HPLC indicated that the silylated intermediate had
converted to the prodrug. The mixture was then concentrated in vacuo to a
golden oil. The resulting oil was dissolved in 300 mL of ethyl acetate
and 300 mL of water. After the pH was adjusted to 2.0 with phosphoric
acid, the aqueous layer was extracted with 150 mL of ethyl acetate. The
combined organics were washed with a 4 % sodium bicarbonate solution,
followed by a 15 % brine solution. The organic layer was dried over
sodium sulfate and concentrated in vacuo to give 3 (32.5 g, 96% yield) as
a white foam. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 0.83 (t, 6H), 1.15-1.36 (m,
6H), 1.46-1.55 (m, 2H), 2.60 (dddd, 1H, J=14.4, 9.6, 5.6, 5.6 Hz), (ddd,
1H, J=12.6, 6.2, 3.6 Hz), 3,77-3.81 (m, 1H), 3,87 (dt, 1H, J=8.4, 3.0
Hz), 4.12-4.22 (m, 1H), 5.27 (t, 1H, J=5.6 Hz), 6.15 (t, 1H, J=7.4 Hz),
6.29 (d, 1H, J=6.4 Hz), 7.31 (d, 1H, J=7.2 Hz), 8.23 (d, 1H, J=8.0 Hz),
11.03 (s, 1H). MS (ES): m/z 390.3 = [M+H]+ Anal. Calcd for C17H25F2N3O5:
C, 52.44; H, 6.47; F, 9.76; N, 10.79; O, 20.54. Found: C, 52.33; H, 6.59;
F, 9.10; N, 10.21. IR (KBr; cm-1 ) 3412, 2960, 2935, 2874, 1661, 1558,
and 1489.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM see experimental details
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis, Crystallization, and Biological Evaluation of an Orally Active
Prodrug of Gemcitabine
