$DATUM tert-Butyl 4-(4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinoyl)piperazine-1-carboxylate: EDC
(625 mg, 3.26 mmol) was added to a mixture of 4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinic
acid (8) (727 mg, 2.17 mmol), tert-butyl piperazine-1-carboxylate (810
mg, 4.35 mmol), HOBT (333 mg, 2.17 mmol), and DIPEA(1.52 mL, 8.70 mmol)
in DMF (20 mL). After stirring for 48h, the reaction was concentrated
in-vacuo and the material dissolved in 1:1 DCM/EtOAc. The organics were
washed two times with saturated NaHCO3, once with saturated NaCl, twice
with 5% citric acid in water, once with saturated NaCl, then dried over
Na2SO4 and concentrated. The crude material was chromatographed on SiO2
eluting with 0-100% hexane:EtOAc. The product (1.05 g, 96%) as a sticky
gum. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ ppm 8.25 (s, 1 H) 7.30-7.50 (m, 11 H)
5.27 (d, J=4.02 Hz, 4 H) 3.59 (br. s., 2 H) 3.37-3.50 (m, 4 H) 3.26-3.31
(m, 2 H) 1.42 (s, 9 H). ESI-MS m/z: 504 [M + H]+.
