(3aR,7S,7aS)-7-(4-amino-3-fluorobenzyl)-3-(3-(tert-butyl)benzyl)hexahydro-2H-thio-
pyrano[3,4-d]oxazol-2-one 5,5-dioxide (1.06 g, 2.3 mmol),
N-methylmorpholin (0.507 mL, 4.6 mmol), N,N-dimethylglycine (0.356 g,
3.45 mmol) and T3P®, (2.68 mL, 4.6 mmol, 50% in DMF) in DMF (9.2 mL) was
stirred under argon at 25 °C for 19 h. The reaction mixture was diluted
with EtOAc and washed with sat. NaHCO3 solution, water and brine, dried
over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. 1.20 g (96%) of
N-(4-(((3aR,7S,7aS)-3-(3-(tert-butyl)benzyl)-5,5-dioxido-2-oxohexahydro-2H-
thiopyrano[3,4-d]oxazol-7-yl)methyl)-2-fluorophenyl)-2-(dimethylamino)
acetamide as a colorless amorphous powder. 1H NMR (360 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.48
(br s, 2H), 8.31 (t, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.41-7.34 (m, 1H), 7.33-7.29 (m,
1H), 7.28 (s, 1H), 7.11 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 6.96-6.92 (m, 1H), 6.92-6.90
(m, 1H), 4.55 (d, J = 14.9 Hz, 1H), 4.33 (d, J = 15.2 Hz, 1H), 3.92-3.82
(m, 1H), 3.81-3.72 (m, 1H), 3.19- 2.99 (m, 5H), 2.91-2.60 (m, 4H), 2.43
(s, 6H), 1.32 (s, 9H); LC/MS (ESI, positive ion): m/z 546 (M+H).
