$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
N'-Acetyl-3-bromofuro[2,3-c]pyridine-5-carbohydrazide (31). To a solution
of 30 (1.58 g, 6.53 mmol) and acetohydrazine (611 mg, 7.83 mmol) in DMF
(10 mL) were added EDC (1.50 g, 7.83 mmol) and HOBt (1.06 g, 7.83 mmol),
and the mixture was stirred at room temperature for 2 days. The reaction
mixture was added into water, and precipitated solid was collected to
give 31 (0.55 g, 28%) as a colorless solid.
3-[4-(Methylsulfanyl)phenyl]-1-benzofuran-5-carboxamide (43). The
compound 43 was prepared in a manner similar to that described for 31 in
95% as a colorless solid. 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6) δ 2.54 (3H, s), 7.37 (1H,
brs), 7.41 (2H, d, J = 8.7 Hz), 7.70-7.80 (3H, m), 7.92 (1H, d, J = 8.7
Hz), 8.13 (1H, brs), 8.41 (1H, s), 8.44 (1H, s). Anal. (C16H13NO2S) C, H,
N.
