$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method 8 (8a-f, 9a-i, and 10a-f). 7j,k were
dissolved in anhydrous DMF (8 mL), and to this were added the required
side chains 3a-i (4 equiv) and PyBOP (3 equiv). The mixture was stirred
at room temperature under N2 (g) for 22 h. The DMF was evaporated and the
resulting oil suspended in CHCl3 (20 mL) with sonication. The resulting
precipitate was isolated by filtration; however, when an oily residue
formed, the organic solvent was decanted. In either instance, this crude
material was dissolved in NH3/MeOH (1 M, 3 mL), and the product was
precipitated with 5% NH3 (aq) (30 mL) and isolated by filtration.
1,3-Bis(3-(4-(3-(morpholino)propanamido)phenylcarbamoyl)phenyl)-urea
(9i). Following method 8, 7k (100.0 mg, 0.333 mmol) was reacted with 3i
(332.4 mg, 1.333 mmol) to yield a pale-purple solid (239.2 mg, 0.314
mmol, 94%), which was purified by filtration from boiling MeOH (2 mL).
HPLC (method C) 97%, tR = 17.20 min. Mp 313-315 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
DMSO- d6) δ 10.19 (2H, s), 10.00 (2H, s), 8.92 (2H, s), 7.98 (2H, s),
7.70 (6H, m), 7.56 (6H, m), 7.44 (2H, t, J = 7.9 Hz), 3.59 (8H, t, J =
4.5 Hz), 2.64 (4H, t, J = 7.0 Hz), 2.48 (4H, t, J = 7.1 Hz), 2.42 (8H, m)
ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO- d6) δ 169.8, 165.3, 152.5, 139.7, 135.8,
135.1, 134.4, 128.8, 121.2, 120.9, 120.8, 119.2, 117.7, 66.2, 54.2, 53.0,
33.8 ppm. HRMS m/z calcd C41H46N8O7 [M + H]+ 763.3562, found 763.3539.
