$DATUM (2S,4S)-N1-(Hex-5-en-1-yl)-4-((7-methoxy-8-methyl-2-(4-(trifluoromethyl)thiazol-2-yl)quinolin-4-yl)oxy)-N1-methyl-N2-((1R,2S)-1-(((1-methylcyclopropyl)sulfonyl)-carbamoyl)-2-vinylcyclopropyl)piperidine-1,2-dicarboxamide
(40). O-(Benzotriazol-1-yl)-N,N, N′, N′-tetramethyluronium
tetrafluoroborate (TBTU, 750 g, 2.334 mol) was charged to a mixture of
amine hydrochloride 24 (655.4 g, 2.33 mol) and acid 39 (1.180 kg, 1.94
mol) in DMF (14.4 L) and the batch was cooled to -5-0 °C.
N,N-Diisopropylethylamine (1.034 L, 5.934 mol) was added over 25 min and
the reaction mixture was stirred at 0-5 °C. After 1 h, the mixture was
added to prechilled water (10 °C, 36.2 L), while maintaining a 10-20 °C
temperature range throughout the addition. EtOAc (18.1 L) was charged to
the mixture and the organic layer was separated after 15 minutes. The
aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (13.5 L) and the combined organic
phases were washed consecutively with HCl (aq, 1 N, 8.0 L), HCl (aq, 1 N,
8.0 L) and NaCl (aq, 12% w/w, 8.0 L). A solution of K2CO3 (623 g) in
water (4.5 L) was added to the resultant organic phase and the mixture
was stirred for 1.5 h at 20-25 °C. n-Heptane (18 L) was added to the
mixture and after 30 min the precipitated solids were collected by
filtration and washed with n-heptane/EtOAc 1:1 (6.0 L). The solids were
then digested with EtOAc (23 L) and water (5.5 L) at 20-25 °C and HCl (1
N) was added to the resulting mixture to obtain pH 2. The organic layer
was separated and washed with NaCl (aq, 12% w/w, 8.0 L), dried using
anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and distilled under vacuum at 40-45 °C to give
diene 40 white solid (1528 g, 94% yield from acid 39, 99% LCAP at 254
nm). HPLC (Method B): tR 6.70 minutes. [α]D25 -12.6 (c 0.5, CHCl3). MS
(ESI+) m/z: 833.33 [M + H]+, 1666.58 [2M + H]+. IR (KBr disc, cm-1) νmax:
3359, 3117, 2935, 1711, 1697, 1628, 1611, 1587. 1H NMR δH (400 MHz,
CDCl3): 0.80-0.86 (1H, m, H-33a), 0.88-0.94 (1H, m, H-32a), 1.38-1.48
(3H, m, H-10, H-10a, H-27a), 1.53 (3H, s, CSCH3), 1.58-1.66 (3H, m, H-9,
H-9a, H-33), 1.73-1.79 (1H, m, H-32), 1.99-2.07 (3H, m, H-3a, H-5a,
H-27), 2.09-2.18 (3H, m, H-28, H-11, H-11a), 2.30- 2.35 (1H, m, H-5),
2.52 (1H, dt, J 14.0 Hz, J 4.7 Hz, H-3), 2.71 (3H, s, CH3), 2.99 (3H, s,
NCH3), 3.24 (1H, dt, J 13.7 Hz, J 7.4 Hz, H-8a), 3.45-3.51 (3H, m, H-8,
H-6, H-6a), 4.02 (3H, s, OCH3), 4.18 (1H, t, J 5.3 Hz, H-2), 4.99 (1H,
dd, J 5.8 Hz, J 1.0 Hz, H-13a), 5.04 (1H, dd, J 9.4 Hz, J 1.7 Hz, H-13),
5.16 (1H, dd, J 5.8 Hz, J 1.1 Hz, H-30a), 5.32 (1H, dd, J 9.0 Hz, J 1.0
Hz, H-30), 5.38-5.42 (1H, br-m, H-4), 5.74-5.86 (2H, m, H-29, H-12), 7.29
(1H, d, J 9.2 Hz, H-18), 7.48 (1H, br-s, CONH), 7.59 (1H, s, H-15), 7.87
(1H, s, H-25), 8.07 (1H, d, J 9.1 Hz, H-17), 9.98 (1H, s, NHSO2). 13C NMR
δC (100 MHz, CDCl3): 9.87 (CH3), 12.99 (C-33), 13.98 (C-32), 18.19
(CSCH3), 22.84 (C-27), 25.94 (C-10), 26.81 (C-9), 30.00 (C-5), 31.73
(C-3), 33.34 (C-11), 34.91 (C-28), 36.12 (NCH3), 36.54 (C-31), 41.67
(C-26), 43.82 (C-6), 50.02 (C-8), 56.30 (OCH3), 56.57 (C-2), 70.75 (C-4),
95.58 (C-15), 113.00 (C-18), 114.96 (C-13), 117.12 (C-22), 118.38 (C-30),
120.27 (C-17), 120.45 (1C, q, 1JC-F 268.8 Hz, CF3), 122.17 (C-20), 123.42
(1C, q, 3JC-F 3.1 Hz, C-25), 132.67 (C-29), 138.27 (C-12), 145.59 (1C, q,
2JC-F 37.1 Hz, C-24), 148.60 (C-21), 150.48 (C-14), 158.41 (C-19), 160.88
(C-16), 165.25 (NCON), 167.64 (CONS), 173.16 (C-23), 173.93 (CONMe). 19F
NMR δF (376 MHz, CDCl3): -63.77 (3F, s, CF3). Anal.Calcd for
C39H47F3N6O7S2: C, 56.24; H, 5.69; N, 10.09; F, 6.84; S, 7.70. Found: C,
56.28; H, 5.70; N, 10.06; F, 6.74; S, 7.73.
