$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of amine 11 (300 mg, 0.79 mmol) in acetonitrile (3.0 mL)
were added N-Boc-N-methylalanine (185 mg, 0.090 mmol), DMAP (catalytic),
and EDC (172 mg, 0.09 mmol), and the solution was stirred at room
temperature for 1.5 h. The solution was diluted with CH2Cl2 (50 mL) and
then washed with 1 N HCl(3 × 10 mL), 1 N NaOH (3 × 10 mL), brine (1 × 10
mL), dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated to afford 426 mg (93%) of
12 as a colorless oil, which was used without further purification. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 7.40-7.26 (m, 5H), 5.85-5.67 (m, 1H),
5.61-5.55 (m, 1H), 5.20-5.00 (m, 3H), 4.35-4.21 (m, 2H), 4.20-4.05 (m,
3H), 3.90-3.80 (m, 1H), 3.60-3.45 (m, 2H), 2.35-2.20 (m, 1H), 2.05-1.85
(m, 3H), 1.85-1.45 (m 3H), 1.45-1.35 (m, 1H), 1.10-0.90 (m, 11H),
0.10--0.90 (m, 9H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 171.11, 170.33,
156.85, 156.14, 67.26, 62.59, 59.65, 56.33, 47.88, 39.38, 35.78, 35.52,
33.22, 31.62, 29.81, 29.63, 28.92, 28.29, 26.32, 17.56, -1.54; HRMS (FAB)
m/z 569.3741 (569.3734 calcd for C28H53N4O6Si M + H).
