$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Methyl-4-nitro-3-propyl-1H-pyrazole-5-carboxamide (3). The carboxylic
acid (2) (1 kg, 4.69mol) was slurried in toluene (5 L) and a catalytic
quantity of dimethylformamide (37 mL) was added. The mixture was heated
to 50 °C and thionyl chloride (0.544 L, 7.5 mol) added over 10 min. On
completion of the addition the reaction was stirred and heated for 55-60
°C for 6 h. The mixture was distilled under vacuum (vessel temperature 55
to 65 °C) until 0.5 L of solvent had been removed. The mixture was cooled
to 20 °C and cold (5 °C) concentrated ammonia solution (6 L) added over
100 min. The precipitated product was granulated, collected by
filtration, washed with water (2 x 2 L), and dried at 50 °C. Off white
solid, yield 0.92 kg, 92.3%. Mp 140-42 °C (lit.3 141-143 °C). 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 1.02 (3H, t), 1.74 (2H, hextet), 2.90 (2H, t), 4.07 (3H, s),
6.13 [1H, s (br)], 7.52 [1H, s(br)].
