$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM MK-1220. To 160 mL DMF under nitrogen was added 1-HCl (32.0 g, 53.0 mmol,
based on assay), side chain 2-TsOH (23.3 g, 58.0 mmol), 2-hydroxypyridine
N-oxide (HOPO, 6.4 g, 58 mmol). The slurry was cooled to 10 °C, and
diisopropylethylamine (DIPEA, 21.0 g, 159 mmol) was added dropwise, while
keeping the batch temperature below 20 °C, and the slurry became a clear
solution. N-(3-Dimethylaminopropyl)-N′-ethylcarbodiimide hydrochloride
(EDC, 14.2 g, 74.2 mmol) was then charged, and the batch was aged
overnight at rt. HPLC indicated 97% conversion and 94% assay yield. The
batch was cooled to 5 °C and charged with IPAc (380 mL) followed by water
(320 mL). The layers were cut, and the aqueous layer was re-extracted
with IPAc (250 mL, then 160 mL). The yield loss in the aqueous layer was
<2%, and the pH of the aqueous layer was ~8. The combined organic layer
was washed with 10% citric acid (180 mL), followed by 5% brine (20 mL)
and water (320 mL). HPLC assay of the IPAc layer indicated 37.4 g MK-1220
(91% yield). The solvent was switched to ethanol by distillation and to a
final concentration of ~0.2 g MK-1220/g and used for the potassium salt
formation.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM product further converted into potassium salt
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Practical Synthesis of A Macrocyclic HCV Protease Inhibitor: A
High-Yielding Macrolactam Formation
