$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Boc-Glu(OBn)-Gly-OtBu (7). To an ice cold CH2Cl2 (25 mL) solution of
Boc-Glutamic acid 5-benzyl ester (3.00 g, 8.90 mmol), HOBt ( 1.44 g,
10.68 mmol), EDC (2.05 g, 10.68 mmol), HCl.Gly-OtBu (2.23 g, 13.35 mmol)
and NMM (2.93 mL, 26.70 mmol) were added and the reaction mixture was
allowed to warm to room temperature overnight. The reaction mixture was
then diluted with dichloromethane (20 mL) and washed consecutively with
10% citric acid solution (30 mL), sat. NaHCO3 solution (2 × 20 mL) and
brine; dried over Na2SO4 and the residue obtained after evaporation of
CH2Cl2 was purified by column chromatography with 20% EtOAc/hexanes to
isolate amide 7 as a colorless oil (3.64 g, 91% yield). R f 0.45
(EtOAc/hexanes, 1:2); [α]D −5.6 (c 0.5, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.37– 7.28 (m, 5H, Ar), 6.83 (s, 1H, NH), 5.41 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H, NH),
5.10 (s, 2H, CH 2Ph), 4.24 (q, J = 7.2, 4.5 Hz, 1H, α-CH:Glu), 3.97–3.81
(m, 2H, CH 2:Gly), 2.59–2.39 (m, 2H, γ-CH 2:Glu), 2.23–2.09 (m, 1H, β-CH
AHB:Glu), 2.05–1.87 (m, 1H, β-CHA H B:Glu), 1.43, 1.40 (2s, 18H, C(CH
3)3); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.2 (COOBn), 171.9 (C(=O)NHGly), 168.7
(COOtBu), 155.8 (C(=O)NH), 135.9, 128.7, 128.44, 128.40 (C Ar), 82.4,
80.3 (C(CH3)3), 66.8 (CH2Ph), 53.9 (α-C), 42.3 (CH2:Gly),30.8 (γ-C),
28.7, 28.4 (C(CH3)3), 28.3 (β-C); ESI-HRMS m/z 473.2260 (M+Na)+,
C23H34N2O7 + Na+ requires 473.2264.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
